  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AI-powered preparedness and anticipatory action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In an increasingly unpredictable global landscape marked by escalating humanitarian crises, IOM underscores the urgent need to shift from reactive to proactive humanitarian action. The growing frequency and intensity of climate-related hazards, conflict, and socio-economic shocks are driving increasingly complex patterns of human mobility worldwide. While traditional humanitarian responses remain essential, they are often constrained by the speed, scale, and compounding nature of these crises, resulting in preventable suffering and inefficiencies. This project aims to strengthen IOM&apos;s capacity to anticipate and act before crises escalate by establishing a lean, Artificially Intelligence (AI)-enabled risk monitoring and analysis capability. The core objective is to deliver rapid, integrated data and actionable insights that support conflict-sensitive anticipatory action (AA) and life-saving preparedness measures.</narrative>
  </description>
